     1,
     "<font face=\"Sans Serif\" size=\"3\">Hello, </font><div><font face=\"Sans Serif\" size=\"3\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"Sans Serif\" size=\"3\"><span style=\"color:rgb(13,13,13)\">I wonder if anyone has already tried to show the target point when using the </span><span style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;font-feature-settings:normal;color:rgb(13,13,13);font-weight:600\">plotRefToTarget</span><span style=\"color:rgb(13,13,13)\"> function with </span><span style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;font-feature-settings:normal;color:rgb(13,13,13);font-weight:600\">method = &quot;vector&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(13,13,13)\">. I really don&#39;t know if that&#39;s possible. The method only shows the reference point and not the target point.</span></font><br></div><div><font face=\"Sans Serif\" size=\"3\"><span style=\"color:rgb(13,13,13)\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"Sans Serif\" size=\"3\"><span style=\"color:rgb(13,13,13)\">Thank you in advance, </span></font></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_JHdsMRDwAJ",
   "from": "Adams, Dean [EEOB]",
   "author": "4d71c6e24fb21497",
   "date": "2024-05-20T13:38:48Z",
   "subject": "RE: [geomorph-r-package] plotRefToTarget function",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Emmanuelle,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">One can accomplish this by combining the plotReftoTarget function plus an additional ‘points’ call to superimpose the landmarks for the specimen you want.  Below is an example:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">data(plethodon) <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Y.gpa &lt;- gpagen(plethodon$land)    #GPA-alignment<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">ref &lt;- mshape(Y.gpa$coords)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">P &lt;- plotRefToTarget(ref, Y.gpa$coords[,,1], method = &quot;vector&quot;)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">points(Y.gpa$coords[,,1], pch = 21, bg = &quot;red&quot;)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Best, <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dean<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\">Dr. Dean C. Adams<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\">Distinguished Professor of Evolutionary Biology<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\">Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\">Iowa State University<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:black\"><a href=\"https://faculty.sites.iastate.edu/dcadams/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://faculty.sites.iastate.edu/dcadams/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792483415392000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3b5nTBfQucXqCT2-qKqerl\"><span style=\"color:#0563c1\">https://faculty.sites.iastate.edu/dcadams/</span></a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\">phone: <a href=\"tel:(515)%20294-3834\" value=\"+15152943834\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">515-294-3834</a><u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Emmanuelle Huet<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Saturday, May 18, 2024 7:24 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> geomorph R package &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] plotRefToTarget function<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Sans Serif&quot;,serif\">Hello, </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Sans Serif&quot;,serif;color:#0d0d0d\">I wonder if anyone has already tried to show the target point when using the\r\n<b><span style=\"border:solid #e3e3e3 1.0pt;padding:0in\">plotRefToTarget</span></b> function with\r\n<b><span style=\"border:solid #e3e3e3 1.0pt;padding:0in\">method = &quot;vector&quot;</span></b>. I really don&#39;t know if that&#39;s possible. The method only shows the reference point and not the target point.</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Sans Serif&quot;,serif;color:#0d0d0d\">Thank you in advance,\r\n</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
